+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool calls are checked against the JSON Schema registered with their tool before an executor is allowed to run.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` describing a rejected input and does not invoke the executor when required properties or declared types are invalid ([validated by: rejects invalid required and typed tool input without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
+- Valid input, including properties not listed by the schema, reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once ([validated by: passes valid tool input and unlisted properties through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+- A static schema is compiled at registration, while a function-valued definition is resolved and validated against its current schema on each call ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and resolves dynamic schemas per call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L49)).
+- An uncompilable static schema causes registration to throw and identifies the tool that could not be registered ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable schema at registration with the tool name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L78)).
